                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "So, first of all, I got this game for free as a product key on reddit. But that's besides the point.\n\nLets start with what's bad\n1. The game doesn't tell you at all what to do, which is ok as I don't mind looking through the game to figure out what to do.\n2. The menu is off, but I'm used to it from RPG maker games, it's somewhat like that.\n3. The game has poor animations and textures, at one point in the beginning there is explosions and such but it all looks off and poorly done, will get back to that scene later.\n4. It's not optimized at all, my computer has an AMd 6-core processor and 24 Gigabytes of ram, along with a good video card and such, and I was lagging hard, getting only 15-20 frames a second, with the medication I'm on for a bas sickness I've been having, I got very sick from playing the game and couldn't play anymore.\n5. During the explosion sequence, there was literally next to no sound, and it was very quiet. There is no sound except for heavy breathing, not very great.\n6. There is no idea on what to do as there is no way to know, you just kept running on the pathway, hoping something would happen.\n7. Adding on to that, for a large portion of the beginning there is nothing to do but run here, press button, run here now, press button, and repeat. \n\nPros\nCan't really think of anything, but it might get better or good much later? Couldn't make it that far though if so.\n\n\nI got this for free, so you might say my statement is invalid, but I really wouldn't spend my money on this, it has many issues and I couldn't even play it.\n\n\n-Echology",
